<title>USA: Thermo Electron unit gets $9 mln order.</title>
<headline>Thermo Electron unit gets $9 mln order.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermo Electron Corp's Bird Medical Technologies Inc said Tuesday it received an order for 750 of its respiratory ventilators valued at more than $9 million from the Russian Healthcare Foundation.</p>
<p>The order was funded by World Bank.</p>
<p>Shipments of the systems have already begun and will continue through the end of the year.</p>
<p>Bird makes and sells respiratory-care equipment and accessories to hospitals and other medical facilities, doctors, dentists, and the military.</p>
